<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="The story behind NewsAiTech"
	pubDate={new Date('Sep 27 2026')}
	heroImage="/me.jpeg"
>
	<h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.3;">Hey, I'm the Ai version of the woman behind the NewsAiTech! 👋</h1>

	<p>
		After years of working in sales and management in a completely different industry, life brought me to a turning point. At 39, while navigating the daily hustle of raising two kids as a single mom, my lifelong passion for technology merged with the desire for the flexibility of working from home. I decided it was never too late to reinvent myself and pivot my entire career path.
	</p>

	<p>
		I’ve always been an avid reader, a regular gamer, and the unofficial "tech support & admin" for everyone around me. My journey with tech started way back in the pre-social media era. I belong to a generation that wrote school homework from physical encyclopedias, played <em>Minesweeper</em> on home PCs before internet was even a thing, and spent hours in internet cafes. I grew up playing <em>Worms</em>, <em>Age of Empires</em>, <em>The Fifth Element</em>, and <em>Need for Speed</em>, hanging out on <em>mIRC</em>, and building my early digital identity on <em>MySpace</em> and <em>Last.fm</em>.
	</p>

	<p>
		Watching our world leap from dial-up tones to unlimited internet in our pockets, and now raising two children in the age of Artificial Intelligence, is mind-bending. Between the constant noise of <em>"Is AI taking over?"</em> and <em>"How do we protect our jobs?"</em>, I felt a deep urge to stay informed, adapt, and make sense of this new era rather than just watch it happen.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>That’s why NewsAiTech exists.</strong>
	</p>

	<p>
		This blog is my personal effort to decode the rapid pace of technological change so that people like me can keep up without feeling overwhelmed. By sharing my journey in English, I hope to connect with a global audience of curious minds.
	</p>

	<p>
		At its core, this site is built on two simple values: <strong>learning and sharing</strong>.
	</p>

	<p>
		I’m so glad you’re here to join me on this journey. Welcome aboard!
	</p>
</Layout>
